# Security and content-type rules for the static site.
#
# Workers static assets parse this file into the deploy metadata and
# apply the rules to responses. They do not serve the file. If
# https://reddmunro.com/_headers returns 200, the last upload did not
# parse it (the file was stored as an ordinary asset). Redeploy with
# Wrangler 4: `npx wrangler@4 deploy` from the repo root, after
# `python build_demo.py`. Do not upload demo/ from the dashboard.
# The diagnosis and the check commands are in docs/DEPLOY.md.
#
# Content-Security-Policy allows this origin plus the two CDNs the page
# actually loads Pyodide from: cdn.jsdelivr.net, and unpkg.com as the
# fallback. 'unsafe-inline' is the page's own script and style blocks.
# 'unsafe-eval' and 'wasm-unsafe-eval' are what Pyodide 0.26 needs to
# compile WebAssembly. blob: is the worker it starts. connect-src is
# the same list, so a dropped CSV has nowhere to go.
#
# The same policy is in the <meta http-equiv> on index.html, minus
# frame-ancestors, which a meta tag is not allowed to set. The header
# is what applies it to every response, including signal_audit.py.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://unpkg.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://unpkg.com; font-src 'self'; worker-src 'self' blob:; child-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'

/signal_audit.py
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300

/*.csv
  Content-Type: text/csv; charset=utf-8

/domains/*
  Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
